#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:21
msgid "Discover Series features and identifiers"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:21
msgid "Discover the native series taxonomy, Series Categories, supported post types, publishing and active Pro addons. Layout discovery uses get-layout; settings use get-plugin-settings. Hub supplies generic post lookup."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:22
msgid "Find Series and Series Categories"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:22
msgid "Find native Series terms or Series Categories by name. Returns native term metadata and concurrency tokens without exposing post content."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:23
msgid "Read posts in a Series"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:23
msgid "List readable posts with their native part numbers, pending order, status and date. Pagination filters unreadable objects first. Get-post-series supplies edit tokens for individual posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:24
msgid "Inspect a Series or category"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:24
msgid "Read name, description, icon, order, category assignments and expected_hash. Series Categories use taxonomy=category. Parent IDs apply to hierarchical categories."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:25
msgid "Create or update a Series or category"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:25
msgid "Create with name, or patch an existing id and expected_hash. Omitted fields remain unchanged. icon_id is a readable image attachment; zero clears the Series icon. category_ids replace Series category assignments; [] clears them. dry_run previews."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:26
msgid "Delete a Series or category"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:26
msgid "Delete a native taxonomy term without deleting its posts. Requires the current term and membership token and permission to edit all affected posts. dry_run previews. Large collections remain in native administration."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:27
msgid "Inspect a post’s Series and block assignments"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:27
msgid "Read Series membership, part numbers, widget short title and Series Gutenberg block attributes for a readable editable supported post. Returns expected_hash covering affected Series order and content."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:28
msgid "Set post Series, part numbers and widget title"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:28
msgid "Replace memberships with items; [] removes all. Omit items to update only short_title. Part zero uses native automatic placement. Multiple Series requires active Pro Multiple Series. All posts whose numbering can change require native read/edit permission. Read expected_hash from get-series before adding a new membership. dry_run previews."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:31
msgid "Update Series memberships for multiple posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:31
msgid "Validate every explicit post, Series token and native permission before updating up to 20 posts. Each row uses the same input as update-post-series. Omitted fields are preserved. dry_run previews all rows. Native numbering is not transactional; inspect complete, applied_ids and failed_id before retrying a partial result."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:32
msgid "Order, publish, schedule or unpublish Series posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:32
msgid "Native Series Order and Publish Series workflows. Get expected_hash from get-series. order requires the complete counted post set and never publishes drafts. pending-order requires complete unpublished set. publish accepts selected pending/draft posts; date is optional site-local YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM for scheduling. unpublish affects the entire Series. trash requires explicit post_ids and native deletion capabilities. mark-published changes only the Series marker. date-asc/date-desc reuse native publication-date ordering. Cross-Series status transitions require series_tokens from get-series for the other memberships. sync-menu-order copies part numbers to WordPress menu order. All affected objects are preflighted; native multi-step operations are not transactional. dry_run previews."
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:33
msgid "Add or configure a Series Gutenberg block"
msgstr ""

#: includes-core/Mcp/Content.php:33
msgid "Append a native Series block or update one using its zero-based path from get-post-series. Only registered Series block attributes are accepted, with native editor availability and layout access checks. No arbitrary HTML or other block edits. dry_run previews."
msgstr ""

